---
import CourseHome from '../../../../components/course/CourseHome.astro';
import { GRE } from '../../../../courses/gre/syllabus';
import '../../../../styles/lesson-kit.css';
---
<CourseHome course={GRE}>
  <section class="cs-builds">
    <h2>Prepare alone, from zero to test day</h2>
    <p>This course follows the shorter GRE General Test (since September 2023): one Issue essay, two Verbal sections and two Quant sections in under two hours. Work through it in order: every lesson builds on the one before, and nothing is assumed.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Learn the GRE's own formats.</strong> Quantitative Comparison, numeric entry, select-all, Text Completion and Sentence Equivalence each get their own method, shown step by step.</li>
      <li><strong>See why it works.</strong> Pictures and short animations show what a triangle rule, a normal curve or a weak argument actually looks like.</li>
      <li><strong>Practise without running out.</strong> Question sets draw fresh numbers every time, with an instant check and a full worked solution.</li>
      <li><strong>Write the essay with a plan.</strong> Module 8 turns the 30-minute Issue task into a five-minute plan and a repeatable paragraph shape.</li>
      <li><strong>Test yourself like the real thing.</strong> Lesson 9.2 is a timed practice test of both Verbal and both Quant sections, with every solution and your weakest topics at the end.</li>
      <li><strong>Take it with you.</strong> Each lesson prints as a one-page summary sheet (save it as a PDF).</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>How long it takes:</strong> 6, 10 or 14 weeks, depending on how much time you have each day. Lesson 1.3 gives a week-by-week plan for each. Tick each lesson as you finish it; your ticks stay in this browser, and you can save them to a file below so you never lose your place. Already taking the GMAT too? The <a href="/learn/courses/gmat/">GMAT course</a> shares the Quant and argument lessons.</p>
    <p class="cs-small">Independent free course, not part of or endorsed by ETS. GRE is a registered trademark of ETS. Every question here is original.</p>
  </section>
</CourseHome>
